{"name":"Scalloped Potatoes","hex":"#f6d58b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"scalloped","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of scallop"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an edge or border marked with semicircles.","Cooked gratin; baked in a typical type of sauce, usually with cheese, as a casserole, e.g. scalloped potatoes; scalloped corn"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/scalloped"},{"term":"potatoes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of potato","plural of potatoe"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of potato"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potatoes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gratin","blocks":[{"text":"Gratin is a culinary technique in which a dish is topped with a browned crust, often using breadcrumbs, cheese, or egg. The term may be applied to any dish made using this method. Gratin is usually prepared in a shallow dish. A gratin is baked or cooked under an overhead grill or broiler to form a golden crust on top, and it is often served in its baking dish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Gratin-Dauphinois.jpg/330px-Gratin-Dauphinois.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gratin","wikidata":"Q1412833"},{"title":"Scallop","blocks":[{"text":"Scallop is a common name that encompasses various species of marine bivalve molluscs in the taxonomic family Pectinidae, the scallops. However, this common name is also sometimes applied to species in other closely related families within the superfamily Pectinoidea, which also includes the thorny oysters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Argopecten_irradians.jpg/330px-Argopecten_irradians.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scallop","wikidat